import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/documents.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="About | Crypto Yield Archive" description="Why Crypto Yield Archive exists and what it does not try to be.">
  <header class="document-head">
    <div><p class="kicker">About the archive</p><h1>Crypto Yield Archive</h1><p class="lede">An evidence-based historical registry for crypto lending, Earn, and yield platforms.</p></div>
    <dl class="document-facts"><div><dt>Focus</dt><dd>History</dd></div><div><dt>Primary view</dt><dd>Platform dossier</dd></div><div><dt>Evidence</dt><dd>Visible</dd></div><div><dt>Uncertainty</dt><dd>Preserved</dd></div></dl>
  </header>

  <div class="document-layout">
    <nav class="document-nav" aria-label="About sections"><a href="#what">What CYA is</a><a href="#why">Why it exists</a><a href="#not">What it is not</a><a href="#records">How to read records</a><a href="#improvements">Corrections</a><a href="#disclaimer">Disclaimer</a></nav>
    <article class="document-prose">
      <section id="what" class="document-section"><p class="kicker">01</p><h2>What CYA is</h2><p>CYA tracks what happened after users deposited assets into crypto yield platforms. It focuses on platform history, customer outcome, terms risk, failure chain, products, and supporting evidence.</p><p>Each platform page is intended to function as a dossier rather than a promotional profile.</p></section>
      <section id="why" class="document-section"><p class="kicker">02</p><h2>Why it exists</h2><p>The 2021–2023 crypto lending collapse cycle produced withdrawal pauses, insolvencies, bankruptcies, restructurings, asset-sale attempts, and unresolved customer outcomes across many platforms.</p><p>Those histories are often scattered across news articles, court documents, company notices, and archived pages. CYA brings them into one structured record system.</p></section>
      <section id="not" class="document-section"><p class="kicker">03</p><h2>What CYA is not</h2><ul><li>Not an APY ranking</li><li>Not a yield discovery product</li><li>Not an investment recommendation site</li><li>Not a trading tool</li><li>Not a real-time TVL or market dashboard</li></ul></section>
      <section id="records" class="document-section"><p class="kicker">04</p><h2>How to read records</h2><p>A platform page combines entity facts, chronology, customer outcome, terms risk, evidence, and known uncertainty. An unresolved record can still be useful because the unresolved state is itself part of the historical record.</p><p><a class="archive-link" href="/timeline/">Browse the historical timeline →</a></p></section>
      <section id="improvements" class="document-section"><p class="kicker">05</p><h2>Corrections and source improvements</h2><p>Good corrections identify the affected page and claim, explain what appears wrong or incomplete, and include one or more sources. Official statements, court filings, bankruptcy documents, regulatory notices, and archived pages are preferred.</p><div class="document-actions"><a class="ghost-button" href="/corrections/">Submit correction</a><a class="text-action" href="/source-quality/">Source quality →</a></div></section>
      <section id="disclaimer" class="document-section"><p class="kicker">06</p><h2>Disclaimer</h2><p>CYA is a historical and educational registry. It does not provide investment, legal, tax, or financial advice.</p></section>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
